config I2S_LOONGSON_LS2K0300
	bool "Loongson 2K0300 I2S driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_LOONGSON_LS2K0300_I2S_ENABLED
	select DMA
	help
	  Enable the Loongson 2K0300 I2S controller ("IIS", user manual chapter
	  11) as a stereo, I2S format, master or slave controller.

	  The data path runs on the LSIA DMA controller (the eight channel
	  engine at 0x1612c000): one circular channel per direction over a two
	  block ring, paced by the controller's own data requests, with the
	  half and wrap boundaries arriving as interrupts. i2s_write() blocks
	  only until the engine is done with the ring half it refills. The
	  transmit and receive interrupts of the block itself stay disabled -
	  they report FIFO overflow/underflow, which cannot be used as a
	  pacing signal.
